diff --git a/wiiu/loading_app/README.md b/wiiu/loading_app/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..dcc05ff353eb8c4e95c2f2b3c9b89612bdc44617
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiiu/loading_app/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Cafe native Loading application draft
+
+This is a standalone WUT RPX driver for the existing Cafe Loading path. Its C
+`main` calls the entropy anchor first, then owns `WHBProcInit`, `WHBGfxInit`,
+their shutdown calls, and the WUT process loop. The Rust static library calls
+`entry::main_with_cafe_host` with the existing `CafeLoadingSession` and
+`Gx2LoadingPresenter`. No alternate menu or renderer is introduced.
+
+While loading, Rust polls the session and VPAD on the main thread, consumes
+each `VpadState::poll_with_evidence` sample/touch marker in the same iteration,
+maps touch to the existing `TouchMapper` pointer events, and dispatches those
+events immediately to `CafeLoadingSession`. Each focused frame also sends the
+real `PadState` through `CafeLoadingSession::dispatch_pad_state`, which uses
+Horizon's typed menu-button path; no keyboard events are synthesized. Terminal
+VPAD errors, focus loss, and exit send a neutral pad state. After focus loss or
+a terminal error, held buttons/triggers are ignored until a successful fresh
+VPAD sample reports them neutral; cached/no-sample defaults and touchscreen
+release evidence do not rearm controller input. WUT ProcUI acquire/release
+callbacks inform Rust of focus changes. Touch capture is released on focus
+loss; touch remains blocked until a fresh physical release after focus returns.
+Rendering and VPAD polling pause while backgrounded. The existing presenter
+draws both WHB targets after foreground acquisition and is dropped before
+`WHBGfxShutdown` on normal returns.
+
+Before constructing the presenter or entering Horizon, the driver sets its
+working directory to `/vol/external01/wiiu/apps/HorizonWiiU`. The Cafe std
+filesystem backend mounts the SD card at `/vol/external01` when it initializes
+its FS client. A missing app root returns to C with an actionable `OSReport`
+and still follows the normal WHB/GX2 shutdown path. Resource selection and
+missing-resource reporting remain with Horizon's original options and loading
+logic, including `--resources` and `--game-dir`. The app root is an explicit
+install-layout contract: install the app at that SD path; resource data may be
+provided through the normal Horizon options.
+
+## Native world session locks
+
+Cafe Rust returns `Unsupported` for `File::try_lock`. WUT's FS/FSA interfaces
+do not expose a file lock or an exclusive-open flag. Horizon's native RPX
+reserves each absolute world path, normalized for the SD card's case-insensitive
+filesystem, in a process-wide registry before touching the save. The world
+session owns the reservation until its marker handle closes. The vanilla
+`session.lock` still contains the two-byte snowman marker and can remain
+after a clean shutdown or a crash without keeping the world locked.
+
+The guard coordinates threads within this RPX. Use one Cafe process per save
+and its normal world directory name. Separate processes, alternate mounts,
+and filesystem-specific aliases such as FAT short names have no shared guard.
+The opt-in Cemu diagnostic retains its existing global host lock.
+
+## Known upstream seams still missing
+
+- **Loading-to-Game:** `CafeLoadingSession::status()` reports
+  `ReadyForHandoff`, but `CafeRunOutcome` only returns `Finished` or the
+  retained `Loading` session. There is no public operation to consume
+  `Loading.loaded`/`menu.pending` and continue into the original `Game` loop.
+  This driver therefore keeps the original title running until exit. It does
+  not report Ready as a game handoff.
+- **GamePad world handoff:** original Loading now receives actual VPAD button
+  and trigger samples through its typed pad-state path. Analog sticks are
+  carried in `PadState` but the startup menu currently consumes button edges;
+  the eventual Cafe Game host still needs to poll and route movement/look input.
+- **Entry error cleanup:** `entry::main_with_cafe_host` preserves the common
+  entry logging/crash path, whose error arm calls `std::process::exit`. An
+  error before or during host startup can therefore bypass C's explicit WHB/GX2
+  shutdown and Rust destructors. A fallible entry seam that returns the same
+  error instead of exiting is required for guaranteed native resource cleanup.
+- **Background GPU resources:** WHB owns and reacquires the TV/DRC render
+  targets; the driver does no drawing while its ProcUI release callback says
+  background. The presenter retains its own HUD/panorama resources across that
+  transition and refreshes target dimensions on the next prepare/draw. This
+  lifetime has not been validated on Cafe or Cemu.
+- **Build substrate:** this directory reuses `wiiu/bootstrap/prepare_wut_startup.sh`,
+  `wiiu/package_rpx.cmake`, and `wiiu/loading_host/CMakeLists.txt`. It still
+  requires a Cafe stage1 Rust compiler/sysroot, devkitPro WUT, Cafe GLSL tools,
+  Cargo target dependencies, and scratch overlays/patches for the Horizon
+  dependency graph and Cafe std. Full-client builds need the TLS-key
+  virtualization patch in `wiiu/rust-std-tls`; an unpatched Cafe std previously
+  aborted with `out of TLS keys`. A later Cemu title checkpoint built with the
+  patched sysroot passed that stage. CMake passes WUT headers and PowerPC Cafe
+  ABI flags into this directory and child presenter targets, but does not
+  install or apply external compiler patches.
+
+Cafe resource selection is already adapted in the original `Options::parse`:
+it uses the relative `.local/horizon-client/<version>` default when
+`current_exe()` is unavailable and still honors an explicit `--resources`
+override. See commit `5d04ef9a5`.
+
+## Build and review
+
+From a devkitPro/WSL shell with the reviewed scratch Cafe compiler setup:
+
+```sh
+export HORIZON_WIIU_STD_RUSTC=/path/to/cafe-stage1/bin/rustc
+export DEVKITPRO=/opt/devkitpro
+powerpc-eabi-cmake -S wiiu/loading_app -B /tmp/horizonwiiu-loading-app -G Ninja
+cmake --build /tmp/horizonwiiu-loading-app --parallel
+```
+
+The resulting RPX is
+`/tmp/horizonwiiu-loading-app/horizon_wiiu_loading_app.rpx`. Native CMake
+configure/link was validated with a prebuilt full-client archive. On 2026-11-11,
+the clean RPX (`4924ea2a2e88529878305227f4e4110a83920d822f664ea9b774bf181ff4b2d5`)
+ran in Cemu 2.6's interpreter and reached Horizon's `title.shown` marker while
+the original title frame was presented through GX2. The archived Cemu log is
+`%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-title-draw-interpreter-20261111.log` (SHA-256
+`D23254B58B79D1832E7F7D0AA1204AA488E50A1104FB34F3C0FCCB556055D250`). The same
+RPX also reproducibly exits during Cemu's recompiler run while loading animated
+texture metadata, before `title.shown`; its archived log is
+`%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-title-draw-clean-recompiler-repeat-20261111.log` (SHA-256
+`634409359D43ADC5849A964396B49F410023DC538C882A431308AEB341E11B20`). This
+does not identify a Horizon source fault or a guest instruction address.
+ProcUI focus lifetime and actual Cafe hardware behavior remain unverified.
+Full acceptance still requires Loading-to-Game handoff and Cafe Game
+movement/look input.
diff --git a/wiiu/loading_app/agent-control.md b/wiiu/loading_app/agent-control.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bcc4bbb1686e31e6fadf204125b82c0535466f16
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiiu/loading_app/agent-control.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Agent Control on physical Wii U
+
+## Pair a development PC
+
+1. Connect the Wii U and the PC to the same trusted private LAN. Launch Horizon and wait for the title menu.
+2. On the Wii U, open **Horizon Settings → AI Agent**. With **No AI** off, enable **Agent Control**. The page shows the bound IPv4 address and port and a 32-character pairing code. Keep this page out of photographs, recordings and screen sharing while the code is visible.
+3. On the PC, use a `horizon-ctl` binary built from this version of Horizon. In PowerShell, enter the displayed code at the masked prompt. Replace the example endpoint with the one on the Wii U.
+
+   ```powershell
+   $ctl = 'C:\path\to\horizon-ctl.exe'
+   $endpoint = '192.168.0.25:37121'
+   $code = Read-Host 'Wii U pairing code' -AsSecureString
+   $buffer = [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::SecureStringToBSTR($code)
+   try {
+       $env:HORIZON_CONTROL_PAIRING = [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::PtrToStringBSTR($buffer)
+   } finally {
+       [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ZeroFreeBSTR($buffer)
+       $code.Dispose()
+   }
+   & $ctl --remote $endpoint state
+   & $ctl --remote $endpoint pad status
+   ```
+
+4. Confirm that `state` reports the Wii U's current screen and `pad status` returns controller state. These are read-only checks. `screenshot tv.png` and `screenshot-gamepad gamepad.png` write to the PC when frames are available. During gameplay, `state` also reports position and world information. Use `horizon-ctl help` for commands and platform-specific availability.
+5. Turn off **Agent Control**, turn on **No AI**, or exit the game to close the connection. For a new pairing, enable Agent Control again and use the new endpoint and code. Clear the shell's copy with `Remove-Item Env:HORIZON_CONTROL_PAIRING`.
+
+Each native launch requires local authorization. Start with a read-only state check before sending gameplay input. Only one PC connection is handled at a time. Close an active `horizon-ctl mcp` session before connecting a second client.
+
+## Configure Codex or another MCP client
+
+Codex uses `horizon-ctl` as a **local stdio** MCP server. Add this entry to your local Codex `config.toml` (on Windows, `%USERPROFILE%\.codex\config.toml`). Use the absolute path to the executable and the currently displayed address and port.
+
+```toml
+[mcp_servers.horizon_wiiu]
+command = 'C:\path\to\horizon-ctl.exe'
+args = ['--remote', '192.168.0.25:37121', 'mcp']
+env_vars = ['HORIZON_CONTROL_PAIRING']
+```
+
+Launch `codex` from the PowerShell session where you entered the code. For Codex Desktop or an IDE extension, the local MCP process must inherit that variable from the host that starts it. Restart that host with the variable set, then check `/mcp` and call `state`. In other MCP clients, configure the same command, arguments and environment forwarding. Keep the pairing code out of command arguments and MCP configuration files. [Codex MCP settings](https://developers.openai.com/codex/mcp)
+
+## Choose a fixed address or port
+
+By default Horizon queries the console's assigned private IPv4 address and lets the network stack select a free port. To override the endpoint, put a `control-lan.json` file beside the RPX in the app's game directory. This file contains only the listen address and port. Set `listen` to a private IPv4 address assigned to the console and use port `0` if you want the network stack to choose the port. Apply changes by disabling and re-enabling Agent Control.
+
+```json
+{"listen":"192.168.0.25:37121"}
+```
+
+An invalid address, unavailable port or entropy failure leaves the listener closed. Check the Wii U connection and the optional file, then try enabling Agent Control again.
+
+## Transport and limitations
+
+Cafe generates a fresh 128-bit code from the production system random source on each activation and retains it in memory. The LAN connection uses Horizon's authenticated ChaCha20-Poly1305 framing with fresh session randoms, directional keys and authenticated key confirmation before forwarding commands to the existing server. It provides encryption and integrity. A party that later obtains the same pairing code can decrypt a recorded session from that activation. A party that can reach the port can also occupy the connection temporarily. Keep the service on a trusted private LAN and leave router port forwarding off.
+
+The Wii U shows the code locally for pairing. The SD file, ordinary logs and copied connection details contain no code. Keep the PC environment private to the local account and trusted processes. Turning off Agent Control revokes the current code. Desktop's local socket and Cemu's opt-in loopback development transport are unchanged.
diff --git a/wiiu/loading_app/cmake/prepare_wut_linker.cmake b/wiiu/loading_app/cmake/prepare_wut_linker.cmake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c7c8283d06854634dd487a1c59bf0c009e86b225
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiiu/loading_app/cmake/prepare_wut_linker.cmake
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+foreach(required IN ITEMS WUT_LINKER_SCRIPT WUT_SPECS OUTPUT_LINKER_SCRIPT OUTPUT_SPECS)
+   if(NOT DEFINED ${required})
+      message(FATAL_ERROR "${required} is required")
+   endif()
+endforeach()
+if(NOT EXISTS "${WUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}")
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Installed WUT linker script is missing: ${WUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}")
+endif()
+if(NOT EXISTS "${WUT_SPECS}")
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Installed WUT specs file is missing: ${WUT_SPECS}")
+endif()
+
+file(READ "${WUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}" linker_text)
+file(READ "${WUT_SPECS}" specs_text)
+string(REPLACE "\r\n" "\n" linker_text "${linker_text}")
+string(REPLACE "\r\n" "\n" specs_text "${specs_text}")
+
+# Validate the exact upstream layout before editing: the constructor-range fix
+# depends on this one insertion point and must never silently produce a partial
+# or duplicate linker script after a WUT update.
+set(init_line "KEEP (*(SORT_NONE(.init)))")
+string(FIND "${linker_text}" "${init_line}" init_position)
+if(init_position LESS 0)
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unexpected WUT linker script: missing ${init_line}")
+endif()
+string(LENGTH "${init_line}" init_length)
+math(EXPR init_after "${init_position} + ${init_length}")
+string(SUBSTRING "${linker_text}" ${init_after} -1 linker_remainder)
+string(FIND "${linker_remainder}" "${init_line}" duplicate_init_position)
+if(NOT duplicate_init_position LESS 0)
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unexpected WUT linker script: multiple .init insertion points")
+endif()
+set(crtend_line "*crtend.o(.text .text.*)")
+string(FIND "${linker_text}" "${crtend_line}" existing_crtend_position)
+if(NOT existing_crtend_position LESS 0)
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Installed WUT linker script already contains the crtend placement")
+endif()
+string(REPLACE "${init_line}" "${init_line}\n      ${crtend_line}" local_linker_text "${linker_text}")
+
+# The installed WUT specs must name the expected linker script exactly once;
+# replace only that path while preserving its entry and all other link options.
+set(wut_linker_token "-T %:getenv(DEVKITPRO /wut/share/wut.ld)")
+string(FIND "${specs_text}" "${wut_linker_token}" specs_position)
+if(specs_position LESS 0)
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unexpected WUT specs file: missing ${wut_linker_token}")
+endif()
+string(LENGTH "${wut_linker_token}" specs_token_length)
+math(EXPR specs_after "${specs_position} + ${specs_token_length}")
+string(SUBSTRING "${specs_text}" ${specs_after} -1 specs_remainder)
+string(FIND "${specs_remainder}" "${wut_linker_token}" duplicate_specs_position)
+if(NOT duplicate_specs_position LESS 0)
+   message(FATAL_ERROR "Unexpected WUT specs file: multiple linker-script references")
+endif()
+set(local_linker_token "-T ${OUTPUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}")
+string(REPLACE "${wut_linker_token}" "${local_linker_token}" local_specs_text "${specs_text}")
+
+get_filename_component(output_dir "${OUTPUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}" DIRECTORY)
+file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${output_dir}")
+file(WRITE "${OUTPUT_LINKER_SCRIPT}" "${local_linker_text}")
+file(WRITE "${OUTPUT_SPECS}" "${local_specs_text}")
diff --git a/wiiu/loading_app/main.c b/wiiu/loading_app/main.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a061bd79f0c66796bb3aeb77c1fa364d2395d4ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiiu/loading_app/main.c
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+#include <coreinit/debug.h>
+#include <nn/ac.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <proc_ui/procui.h>
+#include <whb/gfx.h>
+#include <whb/proc.h>
+
+extern void horizon_wiiu_app_entropy_first(void);
+extern int32_t horizon_wiiu_app_run(void);
+extern void horizon_wiiu_memory_init(void);
+extern void horizon_wiiu_memory_report_display_surfaces(void);
+
+static volatile int32_t sFocused = 1;
+
+int32_t horizon_wiiu_assigned_ipv4(uint32_t *out)
+{
+   return NNResult_IsSuccess(ACGetAssignedAddress(out)) ? 0 : -1;
+}
+
+static uint32_t app_acquired(void *context)
+{
+   (void)context;
+   sFocused = 1;
+   return 0;
+}
+
+static uint32_t app_released(void *context)
+{
+   (void)context;
+   sFocused = 0;
+   return 0;
+}
+
+int32_t horizon_wiiu_app_is_running(void)
+{
+   return WHBProcIsRunning() ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+int32_t horizon_wiiu_app_is_focused(void)
+{
+   return sFocused;
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+   /* This must be the first platform operation: it anchors Cafe std entropy. */
+   horizon_wiiu_app_entropy_first();
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: entropy ready\n");
+
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: WHBProcInit begin\n");
+   WHBProcInit();
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: WHBProcInit complete\n");
+   horizon_wiiu_memory_init();
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: WHBGfxInit begin\n");
+   if (!WHBGfxInit()) {
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: WHBGfxInit failed\n");
+      WHBProcShutdown();
+      return 3;
+   }
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: WHBGfxInit complete\n");
+   horizon_wiiu_memory_report_display_surfaces();
+   /* WHB owns target allocation callbacks. These callbacks only publish the
+    * lifecycle state after WHB's ProcUI pump has processed each transition. */
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: ProcUI callback registration begin\n");
+   ProcUIRegisterCallback(PROCUI_CALLBACK_ACQUIRE, app_acquired, NULL, 100);
+   ProcUIRegisterCallback(PROCUI_CALLBACK_RELEASE, app_released, NULL, 100);
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: ProcUI callback registration complete\n");
+
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: Rust app entry begin\n");
+   const int32_t result = horizon_wiiu_app_run();
+   OSReport("Horizon Wii U startup: Rust app entry returned\n");
+   switch (result) {
+   case 0:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: Cafe entry finished\n");
+      break;
+   case 1:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: original title is ready; Game handoff API is unavailable\n");
+      break;
+   case 2:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: original Loading failed\n");
+      break;
+   case 4:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: cannot enter /vol/external01/wiiu/apps/HorizonWiiU; check that the SD card is mounted and the app is installed there\n");
+      break;
+   case 5:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: original local world startup failed; inspect the Cafe log\n");
+      break;
+   case 6:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: original remote server startup failed; inspect the Cafe log\n");
+      break;
+   default:
+      OSReport("Horizon Wii U: native loading presenter setup failed\n");
+      break;
+   }
+
+   /* Rust drops the presenter and Loading outcome before returning here. */
+   WHBGfxShutdown();
+   WHBProcShutdown();
+   return result == 0 ? 0 : 1;
+}
diff --git a/wiiu/loading_app/memory.c b/wiiu/loading_app/memory.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..faec2b778d52d86e716ba678ab519cbce0442154
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiiu/loading_app/memory.c
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+#include <coreinit/debug.h>
+#include <coreinit/memdefaultheap.h>
+#include <coreinit/memexpheap.h>
+#include <coreinit/memheap.h>
+#include <gx2/surface.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <whb/gfx.h>
+
+static MEMHeapHandle default_heap;
+
+void horizon_wiiu_memory_init(void)
+{
+   /* MEM2's base heap can have zero free bytes while a child heap serves
+    * default allocations. Accept the containing heap only after a known
+    * allocation changes its free count. Do this before workers are started. */
+   void *small = MEMAllocFromDefaultHeapEx(64, 64);
+   if (!small) return;
+   MEMHeapHandle heap = MEMFindContainHeap(small);
+   uint32_t before = 0, during = 0, same_heap = 0;
+   if (heap && heap->tag == MEM_EXPANDED_HEAP_TAG &&
+       (heap->flags & MEM_HEAP_FLAG_USE_LOCK)) {
+      before = MEMGetTotalFreeSizeForExpHeap(heap);
+      const uint32_t probe_bytes = 64 * 1024;
+      void *probe = MEMAllocFromDefaultHeapEx(probe_bytes, 64);
+      if (probe) {
+         during = MEMGetTotalFreeSizeForExpHeap(heap);
+         same_heap = MEMFindContainHeap(probe) == heap;
+         if (same_heap && before >= during && before - during >= probe_bytes)
+            default_heap = heap;
+         MEMFreeToDefaultHeap(probe);
+      }
+   }
+   MEMFreeToDefaultHeap(small);
+   if (default_heap) {
+      uint32_t span = (uint32_t)((uintptr_t)default_heap->dataEnd - (uintptr_t)default_heap->dataStart);
+      OSReport("Horizon memory default_heap arena=%u span=%u free=%u largest_64=%u\n",
+               (unsigned)MEMGetArena(default_heap), span,
+               MEMGetTotalFreeSizeForExpHeap(default_heap),
+               MEMGetAllocatableSizeForExpHeapEx(default_heap, 64));
+   } else {
+      OSReport("Horizon memory default_heap=unverified found=%u tag=%08x flags=%08x probe_before=%u probe_during=%u probe_same_heap=%u\n",
+               heap != NULL, heap ? (unsigned)heap->tag : 0, heap ? heap->flags : 0,
+               before, during, same_heap);
+   }
+}
+
+void horizon_wiiu_memory_report(const char *label, uint32_t len, uint32_t live,
+                               uint32_t peak, uint32_t blocks)
+{
+   if (default_heap) {
+      OSReport("Horizon memory %.*s rust_live=%u rust_peak=%u rust_blocks=%u heap_free=%u largest_4=%u largest_64=%u\n",
+               (int)len, label, live, peak, blocks, MEMGetTotalFreeSizeForExpHeap(default_heap),
+               MEMGetAllocatableSizeForExpHeapEx(default_heap, 4),
+               MEMGetAllocatableSizeForExpHeapEx(default_heap, 64));
+   } else {
+      OSReport("Horizon memory %.*s rust_live=%u rust_peak=%u rust_blocks=%u heap_free=unverified\n",
+               (int)len, label, live, peak, blocks);
+   }
+}
+
+void horizon_wiiu_memory_alloc_failure(uint32_t bytes, uint32_t align, uint32_t live,
+                                      uint32_t peak, uint32_t blocks)
+{
+   /* System has returned from the failed allocation and released its heap lock. */
+   if (default_heap) {
+      OSReport("Horizon memory alloc_failed bytes=%u align=%u rust_live=%u rust_peak=%u rust_blocks=%u heap_free=%u largest_aligned=%u\n",
+               bytes, align, live, peak, blocks, MEMGetTotalFreeSizeForExpHeap(default_heap),
+               MEMGetAllocatableSizeForExpHeapEx(default_heap, align < 4 ? 4 : (int)align));
+   } else {
+      OSReport("Horizon memory alloc_failed bytes=%u align=%u rust_live=%u rust_peak=%u rust_blocks=%u heap_free=unverified\n",
+               bytes, align, live, peak, blocks);
+   }
+}
+
+void horizon_wiiu_memory_report_display_surfaces(void)
+{
+   const GX2ColorBuffer *tv = WHBGfxGetTVColourBuffer();
+   const GX2ColorBuffer *drc = WHBGfxGetDRCColourBuffer();
+   const GX2DepthBuffer *tv_depth = WHBGfxGetTVDepthBuffer();
+   const GX2DepthBuffer *drc_depth = WHBGfxGetDRCDepthBuffer();
+   OSReport("Horizon memory gx2_display tv_color=%u tv_depth=%u drc_color=%u drc_depth=%u\n",
+            tv ? tv->surface.imageSize : 0, tv_depth ? tv_depth->surface.imageSize : 0,
+            drc ? drc->surface.imageSize : 0, drc_depth ? drc_depth->surface.imageSize : 0);
+}
